  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DNA Sample Collection Support to Dutch Immigration and Naturalisation Service for Family Reunification (2023-2024)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">After two years of fruitful collaboration between the Dutch Immigration and Naturalisation Service (IND), the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs (MFA) and IOM, the DNA Sample Collection Support for Family Reunification project will be renewed for a third year. IOM will coordinate the DNA collection process according to the established standard operating procedures, in collaboration with (MFA) and (IND). As the backlogs and prognoses of the IND are uncertain for 2023/2024 and likely to fluctuate, IOM is flexible in assessing possibilities in requests from countries other than Lebanon, Turkey, Sudan, Ethiopia and Iran, and therefore includes a caseload based on dossiers. In addition, IOM will facilitate identification interviews for applicants in Lebanon and Sudan.</narrative>
  </description>
